\text{Side length of the square} = \frac{144}{4} = 36 \text{ units}
\]
The square is divided into 4 congruent rectangles, so each rectangle has a length equal to the side length of the square (36 units) and a width equal to one-fourth of the side length of the square: \[
\text{Width of each rectangle} = \frac{36}{4} = 9 \text{ units}
\]
The perimeter of a rectangle is given by the formula \(2 \times (\text{length} + \text{width})\). So, the perimeter of one of the rectangles is: \[
\text{Perimeter of one rectangle} = 2 \times (36 + 9) = 2 \times 45 = 90 \text{ units}
\]
